Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.17,0:00:02.22,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Episode 55: Mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.52,0:00:11.37,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}On Saturday morning Amy Doukas sat on the steps of the secure lab in the sun with her notebook on her knees, and read it back from Sunday to now.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.67,0:00:14.07,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Sunday had been simple, when she looked at it from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.07,0:00:18.67,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}A woman she had seen once through glass had died in a theatre, and a giant had sat down in the seats.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.67,0:00:19.35,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}That was all.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.35,0:00:21.72,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Then she turned the pages and it wasn't simple any more.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.72,0:00:24.41,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}A giant lay on her table every Tuesday and got heavier.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.41,0:00:28.60,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Two women sat by a fire in a place she couldn't find the edge of, and one of them looked at her hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.60,0:00:30.28,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}A fingernail walked.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.64,0:00:37.06,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She had kept it since Wednesday in a locked steel drawer, and every morning it lay at the end of the drawer nearest the door.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.06,0:00:40.26,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}A benefactor knew which floodlight her cave had been under.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.26,0:00:44.89,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}A boy she liked let men beat him with batons, and smiled when it stung.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.25,0:00:51.03,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She had told the dean's office she had no objection to Mr Vardis sitting by the wall on Tuesday.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.03,0:00:53.27,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She wanted to watch him watching.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.60,0:00:59.70,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She closed the book and opened her phone, because the hand's battery was low and she wanted to know how low.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.97,0:01:03.47,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The app was a plain one, made by the company that had fitted the hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.47,0:01:12.93,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It showed the battery and the grip, with a log underneath that nobody ever read, line after line of numbers, the hand reporting to the campus network every few seconds what it had held and how hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.93,0:01:14.53,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Grip, thirty-one per cent.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.53,0:01:15.83,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Battery, eighteen.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.83,0:01:18.00,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She scrolled down out of habit.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.25,0:01:20.54,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}There was a line in the log she hadn't built.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.84,0:01:26.69,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It sat among the numbers as if it belonged there, stamped 03:12 that morning like the rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.69,0:01:30.97,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It was one word, in lower case, with a question mark after it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.24,0:01:32.07,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.39,0:01:33.74,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She looked at it a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.74,0:01:34.87,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Then she scrolled on.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.87,0:01:37.02,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}At 04:12 the same word.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.02,0:01:47.91,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}At 05:12, and 06:12, and every hour since, on the minute, the hand's log had written it again, mother?, in among the grip and the battery, and the last one had come at 09:12, eleven minutes ago, while she sat
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.91,0:01:50.34,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}on the steps reading about a fingernail.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.67,0:01:58.47,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Amy's prosthetic hand, on the campus network, had written one word into its own diagnostic log, and the word was mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.77,0:02:00.49,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She rang the maker's support line.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.49,0:02:03.34,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}A young man in Athens took her serial number and was very patient.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.34,0:02:04.66,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He said the app couldn't write words.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.66,0:02:05.96,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It logged sensor values.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.96,0:02:11.29,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It had no field for text, he said, and no way to put text in one, and she must have a corrupted file, and he would send her a new version.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.29,0:02:16.62,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She asked him what a corrupted file would have to do, by chance, to spell mother with a question mark after it, every hour on the minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.62,0:02:18.75,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He said he would send her a new version.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.02,0:02:23.07,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}At noon she walked across the campus to the building with no name on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.34,0:02:25.91,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The door let her in on her badge, which surprised her.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.91,0:02:33.26,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She climbed to the third floor, where a man sat alone in a room with the blinds down and four screens lit, with a packet of crackers beside his keyboard.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.26,0:02:41.44,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She had seen his name at the bottom of the overnight summaries that came round to the students, Sotiris Malamas, and once on a ticket about a fogged camera.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.74,0:02:43.52,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He didn't look pleased to see her.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.52,0:02:49.22,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He looked at her phone when she held it out, and at the line on the screen, for perhaps two seconds.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.52,0:02:50.72,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Data leak," he said.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.72,0:02:54.54,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Something on the campus network is writing strings into device logs.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.54,0:02:57.23,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}We've had it in the lab files, we've had it in the console.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.23,0:02:58.67,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It's a known fault."
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.67,0:02:59.81,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He gave the phone back.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.81,0:03:00.87,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"It's not your hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.87,0:03:02.67,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Your hand's fine."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.92,0:03:04.27,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Will you look at it?"
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.52,0:03:07.97,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I'm looking at it," Sotiris said, and turned back to his screens.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.97,0:03:09.49,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"It's on the list."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.84,0:03:12.76,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She went down the stairs with the phone in her good hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.76,0:03:17.72,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Halfway down it buzzed against her palm, and she looked, and it was 13:12.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.99,0:03:23.24,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}On Sunday afternoon she sat on the seawall below the old quarter with Professor Scott.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.54,0:03:31.59,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The wall ran along the edge of the protected coast, where the university could never build, and the sea came in grey and slow over the stones below it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.59,0:03:34.89,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Scott sat with his stick across his knees and his collar up.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.89,0:03:37.04,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He looked better than he had a week before.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.04,0:03:40.34,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He looked as if he had slept one night out of the seven.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.59,0:03:42.04,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Tell me where we are," he said.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.04,0:03:42.89,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"You keep a list.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.89,0:03:44.19,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Read it to me."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.47,0:03:47.72,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}So she did, because it was easier to say it as a list.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.04,0:03:50.77,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Urania made a vow at the dig, over my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.77,0:03:53.62,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}If I won't listen to them she'll give it back to me herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.62,0:03:55.47,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}As the last thing she does."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.47,0:03:56.89,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Amy looked at the sea.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.89,0:03:58.86,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Nobody will tell me what that means.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.86,0:03:59.57,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Clio won't.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.57,0:04:00.23,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}You won't.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.23,0:04:02.19,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Nobody spells it out."
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.47,0:04:03.87,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Scott said nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.12,0:04:07.32,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"The giant has Sofia Andreou's paper in the dean's office.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.32,0:04:11.32,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}If he signs it he gets a roof and a name, and nobody comes up the road with shields.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.32,0:04:14.12,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}If he doesn't, the security firm comes back, and they bring more.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.12,0:04:15.89,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}They told the dean they'd bring more."
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.89,0:04:17.78,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She turned a page she didn't need to turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.78,0:04:22.49,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"And the man who knows which floodlight my cave was under wants to sit and watch him heal."
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.74,0:04:23.79,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"And you?"
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.07,0:04:27.02,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I'm hoping for an explanation I can publish."
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.02,0:04:28.36,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She closed the notebook.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.36,0:04:29.62,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"And I'm afraid I'm ill.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.62,0:04:30.86,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}That's what I'm afraid of.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.86,0:04:35.69,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}A tumour, or something in my blood, that makes me see fires and hear dead women on recordings.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.69,0:04:36.64,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}I looked it up.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.64,0:04:38.75,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}There are things that do that."
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.99,0:04:40.59,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"There are," Scott agreed.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.87,0:04:42.26,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He was quiet for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.26,0:04:46.22,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}A gull went along the wall and settled, and walked, and went up again.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.52,0:04:51.64,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I've known a great many women like Urania," he said at last, "and none of them made a vow lightly.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.64,0:04:53.05,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The old ones least of all.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.05,0:04:56.50,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}They don't have anything left to make one with except themselves."
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.50,0:04:58.07,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He looked at her sideways.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.07,0:04:59.36,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I'd listen to her, Amy.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.36,0:05:00.94,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}If I were you."
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.19,0:05:03.17,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I believe in numbers," Amy said.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.17,0:05:04.15,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"That's all I've got.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.15,0:05:05.92,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}And the numbers are bad."
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.22,0:05:07.48,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Then tell me this."
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.48,0:05:14.50,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Scott turned the stick slowly on his knees, the way he did when he was asking a question in the lecture hall that he meant to leave hanging.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.50,0:05:16.95,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"What number would make you believe?"
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.32,0:05:20.81,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She thought about it honestly, because he had asked her honestly.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.81,0:05:27.94,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She thought about the scanner's weights and the forty seconds of the pelt and the ninety of his stick, and the bag under the glass jar.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.19,0:05:30.62,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I'll know it," she said, "when I measure it."
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.90,0:05:33.65,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He smiled at that, tiredly, and didn't argue.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.94,0:05:39.51,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}That night she didn't look at the phone until she had brushed her teeth and set the alarm and turned the light out.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.51,0:05:42.19,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Then she looked, because she couldn't not.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.47,0:05:48.60,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}At 23:12 the log had written the word again, mother?, as it had every hour for two days.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.87,0:05:52.64,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Under it, for the first time, on a line of its own, was her name.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.92,0:05:53.77,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}amy?
